    "title": "NASA announced a plan to send a mission to Mars in the early 2030s",
    "text": "The United States plans to send a mission with the astronauts in the early 2030s. This was published by the head of the national aviation and research on the space of the United States (NASA) Sean Duffy in an interview with Fox News.\nWith the help of this mission, the United States wants to win the second space race.\nWe want to go to Mars in the early 30s, and this is very important … It will be more than eight months to fly to Mars, then will need to stay there, then it will be returned, Du Duffy said, emphasizing that to maintain the lives of astronauts in the mission, experience flying to the moon.\nIn the United States, they can cancel NASA's duties to return samples from Mars\nIn June, US scientist Jack Kingdon from the University of California at Santa Barbara proposed a revolutionary method to reduce flight time for fire to 90-104 days with existing technologies. This is two to three times faster than modern Mars missions.\nEarlier on Mars had found traces of his storm past.",
